{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1484857-converting-mummy-to-world-of-darkness","id":1484857,"title":"Converting Mummy to World Of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-24T04:52:02-07:00","id":1484857,"title":"Converting Mummy to World Of Darkness","content":"Someone recently sold me on the idea of Mummy: The Curse and I'd like to give it a try in my friend's upcoming multi-splat World of Darkness campaign. Is there a simple, or even moderately complex, conversion guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T14:52:46-07:00","id":1484894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrtwist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1484857-converting-mummy-to-world-of-darkness#post1484857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone recently sold me on the idea of Mummy: The Curse and I'd like to give it a try in my friend's upcoming multi-splat World of Darkness campaign. Is there a simple, or even moderately complex, conversion guide?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, what do you mean with conversion guide anyway? By World of Darkness do you mean the setting of Masquerade, Apocalypse and Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T15:36:27-07:00","id":1484899,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s already a mummy in WoD, but I guess you could ask your ST if you could use the MtC splat instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T20:19:33-07:00","id":1484930,"title":"","content":"What edition to the Old World of Darkness? First edition Mummy the Curse isn't too dissimilar to 3rd or 4th edition Masquerade (I admit I've avoided 5th edition...not really my jam). Some minor tweaks, of course. Nature and Demeanor replace Virtues and Vices. You'd have to splice up Merits into Backgrounds and Merits. I don't THINK there'd be a problem with using a standard point spread for both of those- I'd probably default to vampire the masquerade for reference on how much a character gets. I'd treat Tomb as another background, but Cult is probably important enough to be a separate thing with its own points given to the player to spend. A mummy without a cult in this game is a serious handicap. Most of the mechanics should transfer over as written I would say. Twilight is not so different conceptually from the Underworld of Wraith: The Oblivion. Flaws work differently but again I don't think introducing them into the conversion and having them function as written like they do in Masquerade will unbalance things. <br /> <br /> I'd recommend First Edition Mummy over Second if you want to pursue this. Much closer to the OWOD rules in my estimation. Shows my biases, though. I still prefer that edition for my Chronicles games anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T23:28:22-07:00","id":1484945,"title":"","content":"So for those of you wondering, the close of First Edition Chronicles had Conversion Guides that helped you convert Requiem, Forsaken, Awakening, and Descent over to Masquerade, Apocalypse, Ascension, and Fallen (Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Demon, respectively), both in terms of setting and in characters. It's a useful thing if you want to play in the World setting but not neccesarily all of it, like say wanting to play in World but wanting to play Mummy: The Curse instead of Mummy: The Resurrection instead.<br /> <br /> Now, as for actual conversion, like others, it depends on how much and in what context yer doing it, but I'm going to be really reductive here and simply say &quot;If you want to play Mummy:The Curse in World, insert total success numbers for a roll and otherwise implement target number shifts as feels appropriate&quot; and yer good.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for the current Paradox games because..............I won't in this context as a strict, personal rule, but for older ones, honestly, you can get away with a lot just by facilitating shifting success numbers and total successes needed and otherwise thinking about EXP more traditionally. Making World gamelines play nice with each other is honestly more homework than implementing a Chronicles game in a World setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T03:16:09-07:00","id":1484954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1484857-converting-mummy-to-world-of-darkness?p=1484894#post1484894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, what do you mean with conversion guide anyway? By World of Darkness do you mean the setting of Masquerade, Apocalypse and Ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that's what I meant. Something for Mummy like the translation guides from a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T04:25:57-07:00","id":1484958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1484857-converting-mummy-to-world-of-darkness?p=1484945#post1484945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for those of you wondering, the close of First Edition Chronicles had Conversion Guides that helped you convert Requiem, Forsaken, Awakening, and Descent over to Masquerade, Apocalypse, Ascension, and Fallen (Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Demon, respectively), both in terms of setting and in characters. It's a useful thing if you want to play in the World setting but not neccesarily all of it, like say wanting to play in World but wanting to play Mummy: The Curse instead of Mummy: The Resurrection instead.<br /> <br /> Now, as for actual conversion, like others, it depends on how much and in what context yer doing it, but I'm going to be really reductive here and simply say &quot;If you want to play Mummy:The Curse in World, insert total success numbers for a roll and otherwise implement target number shifts as feels appropriate&quot; and yer good.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for how much, it's basically to make an Arisen in oWoD. I wanted to see if I could grab Sekhem, Utterances, Pillars, and the various other supernatural attributes of the Arisen and port it over. Maybe I can find one of those translation guides and use them for guidance on the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T10:40:11-07:00","id":1484974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrtwist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1484857-converting-mummy-to-world-of-darkness?p=1484958#post1484958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for how much, it's basically to make an Arisen in oWoD. I wanted to see if I could grab Sekhem, Utterances, Pillars, and the various other supernatural attributes of the Arisen and port it over. Maybe I can find one of those translation guides and use them for guidance on the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of those, I feel like either the Demon or Mage Translation Guides would be the most useful. That asides though, I do stand by the idea the majority is easy with the introduction of the two other slidding scales for handling dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}